> Can you expand on what "intentional personal harassment" includes?

Off the top of my head -- and I _know_ I'm going to leave something out,
if for no other reason than that I've got a lovely head cold right now
and my brain feels as clogged as my sinuses -- I'd say that roughly
speaking it's speech or other acts of expression which

(a) target a specific person or a small and identifiable set of people
(e.g., the members of a specific fraternity) either directly or
indirectly (e.g., derogatory speech about a person's mother can be
construed as being targeted at that person),

(b) can reasonably be expected to reach that person or those people,

(c) either are intended to harass or cause emotional anguish on the part
of the target or which the actor knows or reasonably should know will
have that effect, and

(d)(1) does not constitute reasoned discourse, the expression of
   personal opinion clearly labeled as such, or objective truth which is
   not expressed in a slanted or misleading way, and/or

   (2) if put forth in the context of a limited-topic forum, is not
   relevant or appropriate to that forum.

As I said, that's pretty sloppy and probably incomplete.  There may
already exist better definitions; if so, I'm sure Carl Kadie can post
them here :-).

