satisfactory resolution of this question by simply proclaiming all
posts to USENET or a mailing list of more than 3-4 people to be 
"publication" and forgetting about it.

The problem is that the commercial media have always formed a convenient
buffer between the "immovable object" of freedom-of-expression and the
"irresistible force" of right-to-a-fair-trial-from-an-unbiased-jury.
Both are hallowed principles.  Yet you CAN'T keep the jury unbiased by
forbidding every citizen to speak about the topic to any other.  

