No, such intent should be a "necessary but not sufficient" element of
conviction.  A posting which (a) is appropriate to the topic of the
forum and (b) is not intentionally presented in an inflammatory manner
should not be a violation of the charter even if the person posting it
knows or reasonably should know that it will likely generate heat.

