THE FILE ROOM IS OPEN.

The File Room is an illustrated, on-line archive of cases of cultural
censorship which you can browse as well as add cases.

An artist's project initiated by Muntadas and produced by Randolph Street
Gallery (a non-profit artist run center in Chicago), The File Room is
accessible through Mosaic at the URL:
http://fileroom.aaup.uic.edu/FileRoom/documents/homepage.html

(If you aren't running Mosaic, ask your system administrator how you can
get it or if your system doesn't support SLIP operation, ask how you can
access the text through Lynx or a similar method.)

An introduction and instructions are provided on line, but the following
press release gives the full details on the project. For more info. e-mail
me.

