NetNews Usage Guidelines
 
    NetNews provides a mechanism for reviewing and participating in
discussions involving numerous subjects. It provides an excellent
mechanism for improving communication on the campus and off, but it must
be used responsibly. Under no circumstances should trivial or annoying
messages be posted nor should faked or anonymous userids be used.
 
    NetNews contains a few news groups that contain pictures/discussions
that some may find offensive or obscene. Users are reminded to respect
the rights of others. Please note and follow the guidelines listed below.
 
DO NOT create unapproved, unauthorized news groups.
DO NOT display or print pictures that others might find obscene/offensive. 
DO NOT display or forward text that others might find obscene/offensive.
DO NOT submit annoying or trivial messages to any news group or user.
DO NOT submit harmful or harassing messages to any news group or user.
DO NOT submit messages using a fake or anonymous userid or domain.
 Include your name/userid/domain in all submissions, on- or off-campus.
DO NOT submit commercial, for-profit announcements or advertisements.
DO NOT submit chain letters or shotgun type, widespread postings.
DO NOT tie up computing systems with NetNews if others need to perform
  classroom and research assignments.
 
